le signature.","tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_deadline_heldout.py:48,81 — calls `_run_real_guard_with_blocking_git(tmp_path, \"status\")`; if that wrapper's signature changes to thread the transient/persistent selector, these callers break and are not in Scope."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the concrete default value of GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS (e.g. 3) and the resulting worst-case per-probe wall-time bound (attempts x 5s), so the retry count is a decision, not left to the executor.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.501,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'retry the probe up to GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS times, with no sleep between attempts'","'_run_git_probe gains the bounded retry and GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS' — constant named but value never given","Root cause notes runner reaches 91% of the 5s bound; total worst-case wall time = GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS * 5s, which depends on the unstated count"],"finding":"The plan introduces GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS but never states its value (the retry count / bound), leaving the executor to pick the number.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe3601e5b40a58b43","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope: 'retry the probe up to GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS times'","norm_id":"n2ca92cfcba947f0f","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor guesses attempts=2, which may be too few if contention spikes recur back-to-back","Executor picks a large count, multiplying the worst-case teardown wall-time on an already-45-minute runner"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Set GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS = 3 (worst case 15s per persistent-failure probe) and note it is a module-level constant analogous to GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the concrete GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS value and justify it against the runner budget — note the worst-case persistent-stall cost is attempts × GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS per probe and confirm that bound is acceptable across the ~19,000-probe session.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.501,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope: 'tests/_isolation.py -- _run_git_probe gains the bounded retry and GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS.'","Plan Root cause: 'runs ~19,000 times under -n 3 on a 45-minute macOS runner' and 'reaches 91% of the probe's fixed 5s bound'","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 5 (tests/_isolation.py:31) is per-attempt, so N attempts multiply the persistent-case wall cost"],"finding":"The plan introduces GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS as the retry bound but never states its value or a worst-case-latency rationale; because the probe runs ~19,000 times under -n 3 on a ~45-minute macOS runner and each attempt carries the fixed 5s per-attempt timeout, the worst-case per-probe cost under a genuinely-persistent stall becomes attempts × 5s, which the plan does not bound or justify against the runner budget it cites as already 91%-stressed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f16cd53b6cb1b7284","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (tests/_isolation.py -- _run_git_probe gains the bounded retry and GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS)","norm_id":"n6ea99f7ae45cf4de","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A genuinely persistent stall (real HEAD-probe hang) now costs attempts × 5s before raising, multiplying the worst-case teardown latency across a session that already tops out near the per-probe bound"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reach